ale (Brassica oleracea var. alboglabra) is a leafy vegetable with thick, flat, glossy blue-green leaves with thick stems, and florets similar to (but much smaller than) broccoli. A Brassica oleracea cultivar, gai lan is in the group alboglabra (from Latin albus \"white\" and glabrus \"hairless\"). When gone to flower, its white blossoms resemble that of its cousin Matthiola incana or hoary stock. The flavor is very similar to that of broccoli, but noticeably stronger and slightly more bitter."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-gai-lan"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gai_lan"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Thai cuisine","cuisine/thai-cuisine",[["Pad see ew","dish/pad-see-ew"],["Rad naa","dish/rad-naa"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Noodles","ingredient/noodles"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Shahe fen","ingredient/shahe-fen"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Rice noodles","ingredient/rice-noodles"],["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Cornstarch","ingredient/cornstarch"],["Fish sauce","ingredient/fish-sauce"],["Soy sauce","ingredient/soy-sauce"],["Tapioca","ingredient/tapioca"],["Tofu","ingredient/tofu"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/9/90/Gailan.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Kowloonese","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gailan.jpg"}},"dish/scotch-broth":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/scotch-broth","n":"Scotch broth","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Scottish cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Scotch broth is a soup originating in Scotland. The principal ingredients (fresh or preserved as available) are usually barley, stewing or braising cuts of lamb, mutton or beef, root vegetables (such as carrots, swedes, or sometimes turnips), and dried pulses (most often split peas and red lentils). Cabbage and leeks are often added shortly before serving to preserve their texture, colour and flavours. The proportions and ingredients vary according to the recipe or availability. Scotch broth has been sold ready-prepared in tins for many years."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-scotch-broth"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scotch_broth"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Scottish cuisine","cuisine/scottish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":6,"links":[["Barley","ingredient/barley"],["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Pulse (legume)","ingredient/pulse-legume"],["Rutabaga","ingredient/rutabaga"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Scottish Scran","ref":"site/scottishscran-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"scottishscran.com","note":"Blog working through traditional Scottish dishes one recipe at a time.","url":"https://scottishscran.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Something Sweet Something Savoury: Scottish recipes","ref":"site/somethingsweetsomethingsavoury-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"somethingsweetsomethingsavoury.com","note":"Scottish home baking and cooking section of a UK food blog.","url":"https://somethingsweetsomethingsavoury.com/category/scottish-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Scottish cuisine","links":[["Clootie dumpling","dish/clootie-dumpling"],["Cock-a-leekie","dish/cock-a-leekie"],["Finnan haddie","dish/finnan-haddie"],["Haggis","dish/haggis"],["Haggis pakora","dish/haggis-pakora"],["Hobnob biscuit","dish/hobnob-biscuit"],["Lorne sausage","dish/lorne-sausage"],["Mince and tatties","dish/mince-and-tatties"],["Rumbledethumps","dish/rumbledethumps"],["Skirlie","dish/skirlie"],["Stornoway black pudding","dish/stornoway-black-pudding"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/31/Lunch_at_Inveraray_Castle_-_Scotch_broth_%2814342541740%29.jpg/500px-Lunch_at_Inveraray_Castle_-_Scotch_broth_%2814342